decision_conditions:
Condition : 4 - No development shall take place until a Construction Logistics Plan (CLP), written in accordance with current TfL guidance, has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CLP shall include: 

a)	a site plan (showing the elements set out below);
b)	provision for the parking of vehicles of site operatives and visitors;
c)	provisions for loading, unloading and storage of plant and materials within the site;
d)	a scheme for recycling/disposing of waste resulting from demolition and construction works; 
e)	measures to ensure the safety of all users of the public highway especially cyclists and pedestrians in the vicinity of the site and especially at the access;
f)	commitment to liaise with other contractors in the vicinity of the site to maximise the potential for consolidation and to minimise traffic impacts;
g)	avoidance of peak hours for deliveries and details of a booking system to avoid vehicles waiting on the public highway;
h)	all necessary traffic orders and other permissions required to allow safe access to the site to be secured and implemented prior to commencement of construction;

The approved CLP shall be adhered to throughout the construction period for the development.
